# Cloudflare R2 Storage Architecture

## Storage Priority Chain

All object storage flows through this priority chain:

| Priority | Backend | Egress Cost | Config Check |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Cloudflare R2 | $0 (zero) | `R2_ACCOUNT_ID` + `R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID` + `R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` |
| 2 | Azure Blob | ~$0.087/GB | `AZURE_STORAGE_CONNECTION_STRING` |
| 3 | Local disk | N/A | Always available |

If R2 is not configured, the system falls back to Azure, then local disk — identical to pre-R2 behavior.

## R2 Buckets

| Bucket | Env Var | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `nate-vault` | `R2_DEFAULT_BUCKET` | Vault uploads, general blob storage |
| `nate-warm-memory` | `R2_WARM_BUCKET` | Warm memory tier (session archives, insights) |
| `nate-cold-archive` | `R2_COLD_BUCKET` | Cold memory tier (client history, legacy data) |
| `nate-heritage-vault` | `R2_HERITAGE_BUCKET` | Heritage Vault quad-redundant storage |

